WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.770
In 1815,

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.930
Mount Tambora erupted in Indonesia,

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.757
killing an estimated 92,000 people.

00:00:08.757 --> 00:00:12.550
It was the biggest eruption
in recorded history.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.480
And yet, Tambora was
about one-seventh the size

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.840
of the smallest supervolcano.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.665
There are about a dozen of
these monsters worldwide,

00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:27.665
and the last one went off
26,500 years ago in New Zealand,

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.040
blanketing most of its island
in a layer of thick ash.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.391
Now, it's extremely unlikely

00:00:34.391 --> 00:00:36.160
that one of these supervolcanoes

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.270
would go off anytime soon,

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.677
let alone multiple eruptions at once.

00:00:41.677 --> 00:00:43.565
But, for curiosity's sake,

00:00:43.565 --> 00:00:45.230
what would happen

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.700
if all the world's supervolcanoes

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.649
erupted at once?

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.200
If every supervolcano went off,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.720
you'd have a hard time finding
a safe place to flee to,

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.830
because almost every continent

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.930
is home to at least one supervolcano.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.290
For example, there's
Yellowstone in the US,

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.560
Ngorongoro in Tanzania,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.620
and Toba in Indonesia.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.879
So, basically, no matter where you are,

00:01:14.879 --> 00:01:17.130
you're out of luck.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.740
But at least you'll have a warning,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.270
because weeks or months beforehand,

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.120
the ground will tremble with earthquakes.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.470
Then, when E-Day arrives,

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:30.118
the earth-shattering sound
would be a dead giveaway

00:01:30.118 --> 00:01:32.370
that something wasn't right.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.610
When Krakatoa,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.090
which wasn't even close

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.970
to the size of a supervolcano,

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.054
erupted in 1883,

00:01:39.054 --> 00:01:41.320
it released a roar so loud

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.887
the sound traveled nearly 4,800 kilometers

00:01:44.887 --> 00:01:46.830
across the Indian Ocean,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.463
shattering windows and
deafening people in its path.

00:01:50.463 --> 00:01:52.830
And since even the smallest supereruption

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.070
would dwarf Krakatoa's eruption,

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.570
there is really no telling how
much damage this would cause,

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.840
but it would be epically catastrophic.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.210
And let's say you were
lucky enough to survive

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.370
this first wave of destruction.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:09.920
After that, it would be time
to find a fallout shelter,

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.586
because these supereruptions spew

00:02:12.586 --> 00:02:15.761
billions of tons of ash,
volcanic glass, and rock

00:02:15.761 --> 00:02:18.090
thousands of meters into the air.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:21.989
Not something you want to
inhale or be in the path of,

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:25.447
since this cloud of ash
doesn't just travel up;

00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:27.720
it also expands out,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.210
crashing across the landscape
at jet-fighter speeds.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.031
It would collapse buildings,

00:02:33.031 --> 00:02:35.015
contaminate water supplies,

00:02:35.015 --> 00:02:38.350
and bring down any
power grids in its path.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.030
And the fallout would extend
for hundreds of kilometers,

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.030
so any cities nearby a
supervolcano are immediately toast.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.220
As are any planes that attempt

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.060
to fly people away from the danger.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.930
And keep in mind that ash travels.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.430
When Toba erupted 74,000 years ago,

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:02.045
winds blew ash all the way to India.

00:03:02.045 --> 00:03:04.880
So if all the supervolcanoes
go off at once,

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.590
volcanic debris would
spread across the globe.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.020
When the eruption ends,

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.040
the disaster will have only just started.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.240
Because for the next six months,

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.130
much of that supervolcanic ash

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.420
would linger in the
stratosphere and block sunlight,

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.490
causing global temperatures to plunge

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.924
by as much as 15 degrees Celsius.

00:03:25.924 --> 00:03:29.360
That's close to the difference
between summer in Rio

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.630
versus Anchorage, Alaska.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.090
In fact, just "little"
Mount Tambora's eruption

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.320
alone set off the "Year Without a Summer,"

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.847
where frost and blizzards plagued much

00:03:40.847 --> 00:03:42.350
of the Northern Hemisphere.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:45.850
So, multiply that by the
12 or so supervolcanoes

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:48.461
all spewing thick black dust,

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.730
and you've got a worldwide volcanic winter

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.410
for the next few years.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.660
Tropical forests,

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.410
which can't handle cold weather,

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.140
would wither and die,

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.740
bringing down the
millions of animal species

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.250
that live there.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:06.661
And it's about to get even bleaker.

00:04:06.661 --> 00:04:07.660
You know that saying

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.270
"out of the frying pan and into the fire"?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.545
Well, in addition to ash,

00:04:12.545 --> 00:04:15.440
those volcanoes also belch toxic gasses,

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.490
like sulfur dioxide, into the atmosphere.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.811
And after a few years,

00:04:19.811 --> 00:04:22.997
just after the winter finally ends,

00:04:22.997 --> 00:04:27.970
those gasses would start to
fall from the sky as acid rain.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:32.250
When the Laki volcano
erupted in 1783 in Iceland,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.030
it rained down so much sulfuric acid

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.740
that it devastated farmland

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.810
and wiped out half of all livestock.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:40.960
The next year,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.180
a full quarter of
Iceland's population died

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.110
in the resulting famine.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.510
So imagine that,

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.460
but everywhere.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:52.440
And since Laki wasn't even a supervolcano,

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.290
we're looking at acid
rain for the next decade.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.224
Say goodbye to civilization,

00:04:58.224 --> 00:05:00.300
because it probably can't survive

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.940
a decade-long global famine.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.440
Now, there are a few places on Earth

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.750
that, while still suffering from cold

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.600
and acid rain and famine,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.880
would at least be free

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.970
from the actual explosions themselves.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.878
Like volcanic islands
such as the Galapagos,

00:05:16.878 --> 00:05:18.527
or even Hawaii,

00:05:18.527 --> 00:05:22.690
which ironically is
famous for its volcanoes.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.100
But the thing is,

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:27.380
these volcanoes slowly
release flows of lava

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.260
rather than violently exploding.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.880
So, you could at least enjoy a nice view

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.963
as civilization implodes.

